Today's iPadOS 27.3 and macOS 27.3 betas expand <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a> support in China to the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad/">iPad</a> and the Mac.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2024/09/Apple-Intelligence-General-Feature-2.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-963424" /><br/>
&zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj; features <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/03/ios-27-3-apple-intelligence-china-2/">debuted in China</a> on the iPhone in the first iOS 27.3 beta, but they weren't initially available in iPadOS 27.3 or macOS 27.3. The Shanghai Cyberspace Administration <a href="https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s/hg779MxQS-tnjxzAfDyZXg">said on November 9</a> that Apple had registered to bring &zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj; to tablets and laptops.<br/>
<br/>
Developers in China can test &zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj; after updating to the second iPadOS 27.3 and macOS 27.3 betas. &zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj; is available on Macs and iPads with an M-series Apple silicon chip, as well as the A17 Pro and A20 Pro &zwnj;iPad&zwnj; minis.<br/>
<br/>
&zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj; in China does not include <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI, the &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; app, or the newer &zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj; features in <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a>, but it does include many of the features that debuted in the U.S. starting in iOS 18.1. &zwnj;Siri&zwnj;, Writing Tools, and other features integrate with Alibaba's Qwen model, similar to the ChatGPT integration in other countries.<br/>
<br/>
Here's what's live:<br/>
<ul><br/>
 	<li>Live Translation for Messages, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/facetime/">FaceTime</a>, and the Phone app. Live Translation also works with AirPods 4 with ANC, AirPods Pro 2, and later models.</li><br/>
 	<li>Writing Tools for rewriting, proofreading, and summarizing text. With Qwen integration, users can also generate text.</li><br/>
 	<li><a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/visual-intelligence/">Visual Intelligence</a> for identifying objects, places, and more.</li><br/>
 	<li>Clean Up in <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/photos/">Photos</a> for removing unwanted objects from images.</li><br/>
 	<li><a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/genmoji/">Genmoji</a> for creating custom emoji.</li><br/>
 	<li>Natural language search and memory movie creation in &zwnj;Photos&zwnj;.</li><br/>
 	<li>Email summaries, suggested smart replies, and priority emails in the Mail app.</li><br/>
 	<li>Notification summaries, urgent notifications, and the Reduce Interruptions Focus mode.</li><br/>
 	<li>Summaries for audio recordings in the Notes app.</li><br/>
 	<li>Call transcripts in the Phone app, which are saved to the Notes app.</li><br/>
 	<li>Type to &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; and more natural &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; responses.</li><br/>
 	<li>&zwnj;Siri&zwnj; can relay requests to Qwen to give more in-depth answers.</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
